<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Korean text for Prayer Gate. EDIT THIS FILE, not res/values-ko/strings.xml.

    After editing, run:  python3 tools/make_strings_ko.py
    The script copies this file to app/src/main/res/values-ko/strings.xml and
    glues the letters of each Korean word together with an invisible
    "word joiner", so Android wraps lines between words, not inside them.

    Style:
    - Words of faith follow Korean Protestant usage: 하나님, 기도, 아멘, 말씀.
      The prayers themselves (assets/prayers.json) use the reverent -소서 form.
    - Buttons and settings use standard UI forms: -하기, 변경, 사용 안 함,
      전체, 탭하여, ~개 선택됨, 실행 중.
    - Help and onboarding text use polite 해요체. Legal text uses 합니다체.
    - Settings names follow the words Samsung uses in its own Korean settings
      screens (사용 정보 접근, 다른 앱 위에 표시, 제한된 설정, 절전 예외 앱),
      so the instructions match what people see on their phones.
    - "Prayer Gate" stays in English. It ends in a vowel sound (게이트), so it
      takes 가 / 를 / 는.
    Keep the name="..." parts and the %1$s / %1$d placeholders exactly as they are.
-->
